    <summary>Lightweight snipping tool that stacks screenshots into a running list per tab.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
MultiSnip is a small screenshot tool for Windows, written in plain C++ against the
Win32 API. Instead of handing you one capture at a time, it stacks every snip
underneath the previous one into a running list, so a bug report, a how-to or a
comparison grows as you work. Each snip stays individually manageable, and the
whole stack can be copied or exported as a single image.

### Features

* **Stacked captures** - new snips append to the current tab; reorder them by
  dragging, hide, replace or delete single entries.
* **Tabs** - several independent stacks side by side, each with its own
  background colour, border, spacing, capture delay (0-10 s) and copy behaviour.
* **Annotation editor** - unlimited layers of vector shapes per snip: pen,
  marker, line, arrow, rectangle, ellipse, text, numbered badges and crop.
  The PNG is never touched; shapes live in a sidecar file and are rendered into
  preview, clipboard and export.
* **Text recognition** - OCR via the Windows text recognition engine, with the
  result in an editable dialog. Needs a Windows language pack that includes OCR.
* **Clipboard and export** - copy the whole stack or a single snip (CF_DIB plus
  PNG), or save the composite as a PNG.
* **Global hotkey** - `Ctrl+PrtScn` by default, plus full keyboard navigation
  and a tray icon.
* **Plain file storage** - snips are PNGs and INI files under
  `%LocalAppData%\MultiSnip`, so nothing is locked into a database.
* **German, English and Spanish** user interface.

### Notes

* Requires Windows 10 version 1809 (build 17763) or newer.
* Installs per machine into `%ProgramFiles%\MultiSnip`. Settings and snips in
  `%LocalAppData%\MultiSnip` are kept on uninstall.
* The binaries are not code signed, so SmartScreen may warn on first launch.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/BjWe/MultiSnip/releases/tag/v1.1.1</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
